        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I understand your concern about performance, but to provide some context, I think this operation is already executed by default each time a character is typed.\r\nWithout the remapping of `mini.pairs`, this seems to be exactly what Vim does internally when a bracket, space, or any character not in `iskeyword` is entered, so invoking it manually shouldn't differ from the default behavior (this can be observed in the [Vim source code here](https://github.com/vim/vim/blob/a9c6f90918d0012d1b8c8c5c1dccb77407f553fb/src/edit.c#L1373-L1380), though I'm not entirely certain).\r\nThat said, I haven't tested it thoroughly, so I understand if it's a concern, and there may be more efficient approaches!",
