        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Without the remapping of `mini.pairs`, this seems to be exactly what Vim does internally when a bracket, space, or any character not in `iskeyword` is entered, so invoking it manually shouldn't differ from the default behavior (this can be observed in the [Vim source code here](https://github.com/vim/vim/blob/a9c6f90918d0012d1b8c8c5c1dccb77407f553fb/src/edit.c#L1373-L1380), though I'm not entirely certain).\r\n\r\nAnd I think it should still do that even if the character comes as a result of mapping. As in 'mini.pairs' pressing `(` should be fully equivalent to pressing `(`, `)`, and `<Left>`. I'll ask around if this is an unexpected behavior and if yes - file an issue.",
